From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:31:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: tcon: Refuse modes the A733 TCON TV cannot time

The A733 TCON TV writes each timing of a mode into a field of fixed
width, and it times video formats up to 4096x2160 (user manual section
15.2.1, PDF page 723). A mode beyond either limit passes the CRTC, and
the registers take its timings modulo the width of their fields, so the
TCON times another picture than the one the display engine and the
DisplayPort transmitter work on.

Refuse such a mode in the mode_valid hook of the CRTC, for the A733 TCON
TV only: a width above 4096, a height above 2160, and a sync width or
back porch that TV_BASIC3 to TV_BASIC5 cannot hold (sections 15.2.10.9
to 15.2.10.11, PDF pages 747 and 748). The size fields are wider than
the format limits, and the total fields hold every total that a mode can
have, so they need no check. The main stream registers of the
transmitter are wider than the TCON fields (sections 15.4.7.44 to
15.4.7.52, PDF pages 786 to 788) and add no limit.

Not covered: the other TCONs, interlaced modes, which the transmitter
refuses, a limit on the pixel clock, which stays with the output, and
the output size of the display engine. The manual gives it as 4096x2048
(section 14.3, PDF page 662), less than the 2160 lines of the TCON TV.
That limit belongs to the mixer and has not been measured.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board with a DisplayPort
monitor and a mode wider than 4096 pixels forced on the kernel command
line; the mode was refused with MODE_BAD_HVALUE, and the picture came up
in the preferred mode of the monitor.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tcon.c | 44 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tcon.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tcon.c
index bf45edc6a37a..e992df5bceb2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tcon.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tcon.c
@@ -760,6 +760,43 @@ static void sun4i_tcon1_mode_set(struct sun4i_tcon *tcon,
 			   SUN4I_TCON_GCTL_IOMAP_TCON1);
 }
 
+/* The largest video format of the A733 TCON TV (section 15.2.1) */
+#define SUN60I_TCON_TV_MAX_WIDTH	4096
+#define SUN60I_TCON_TV_MAX_HEIGHT	2160
+
+/* The timing fields of the A733 TCON TV hold the timing less one */
+static bool sun60i_tcon_tv_fits(unsigned long mask, unsigned int timing)
+{
+	return timing - 1 <= mask;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The A733 TCON TV cuts a timing off at the width of its field (sections
+ * 15.2.10.8 to 15.2.10.11) and times video formats up to 4096x2160. The
+ * fields of the sizes are wider than that and those of the totals hold
+ * every total a mode can have, so only the size, the sync widths and the
+ * back porches are left to check.
+ */
+static enum drm_mode_status
+sun60i_tcon_tv_mode_valid(const struct drm_display_mode *mode)
+{
+	if (mode->hdisplay > SUN60I_TCON_TV_MAX_WIDTH ||
+	    !sun60i_tcon_tv_fits(SUN60I_TCON1_BASIC5_H_SYNC_MASK,
+				 mode->hsync_end - mode->hsync_start) ||
+	    !sun60i_tcon_tv_fits(SUN60I_TCON1_BASIC3_H_BACKPORCH_MASK,
+				 mode->htotal - mode->hsync_start))
+		return MODE_BAD_HVALUE;
+
+	if (mode->vdisplay > SUN60I_TCON_TV_MAX_HEIGHT ||
+	    !sun60i_tcon_tv_fits(SUN60I_TCON1_BASIC5_V_SYNC_MASK,
+				 mode->vsync_end - mode->vsync_start) ||
+	    !sun60i_tcon_tv_fits(SUN60I_TCON1_BASIC4_V_BACKPORCH_MASK,
+				 mode->vtotal - mode->vsync_start))
+		return MODE_BAD_VVALUE;
+
+	return MODE_OK;
+}
+
 /*
  * Channel 1 is the pixel clock of the TCON. Where the clock tree cannot
  * make the rate of a mode to within the 0.5 % that VESA DMT allows, refuse
@@ -769,8 +806,15 @@ enum drm_mode_status sun4i_tcon_mode_valid(struct sun4i_tcon *tcon,
 					   const struct drm_display_mode *mode)
 {
 	unsigned long clock = mode->clock * HZ_PER_KHZ;
+	enum drm_mode_status status;
 	long rounded;
 
+	if (tcon->quirks->has_tv_layout) {
+		status = sun60i_tcon_tv_mode_valid(mode);
+		if (status != MODE_OK)
+			return status;
+	}
+
 	if (!tcon->quirks->checks_ch1_rate)
 		return MODE_OK;
 
